## 5. CODE EXPLAINED

A. Importing Libraries
- Pandas is used to load and manipulate the dataset.
- train_test_split divides data into training and testing sets.
- StandardScaler standardizes numerical features.

B. Loading and Exploring Data
- read_csv() loads the CSV dataset.
- head() displays the first five rows by default.
- info() displays column names, data types, and non-null counts.
- isnull().sum() counts missing values in each column.

C. Handling Missing Values
- select_dtypes(include="number") selects numerical columns.
- columns returns the names of those columns.
- fillna(0) replaces missing numerical values with zero.
- The dictionary passed to fillna() assigns "None" to selected categorical columns.
- The final fillna("No") fills any remaining missing values with "No".
- In a real project, replacement values should be selected according to what a blank means in each column. Zero, "None", and "No" are not interchangeable in every dataset.

D. Removing Duplicates and Cleaning Text
- drop_duplicates() removes repeated rows.
- select_dtypes(exclude="number") selects non-numerical columns.
- str.strip() removes leading and trailing spaces from text values.
- astype(str) converts Zip Code values to strings so they are treated as identifiers rather than numbers.

E. Handling Outliers Using IQR
- The interquartile range (IQR) is Q3 minus Q1.
- q1 is the 25th percentile and q3 is the 75th percentile.
- The lower limit is Q1 - 1.5 × IQR.
- The upper limit is Q3 + 1.5 × IQR.
- clip() caps values below or above these limits rather than deleting the rows.

F. Feature Engineering
- The Churn column is created from Customer Status.
- A customer with status "Churned" gets 1; other statuses get 0.
- astype(int) converts True/False values into 1/0.
- Tenure Years is calculated by dividing Tenure in Months by 12.

G. Exporting the Cleaned Dataset
- to_csv() saves the cleaned DataFrame to a new CSV file.
- index=False prevents Pandas from writing the row index as an extra column.

H. Separating Features and Target
- X contains the input features used to predict churn.
- y contains the target variable, Churn.
- drop(columns=[...]) removes identifiers and columns excluded from model input.

I. Encoding Categorical Variables
- Machine learning algorithms generally require numerical input.
- get_dummies() converts categorical columns into indicator columns.
- drop_first=True removes one category from each encoded group to reduce redundant columns.

J. Splitting the Dataset
- train_test_split() divides the data into training and testing sets.
- test_size=0.2 assigns 20% to testing and 80% to training.
- random_state=42 makes the split reproducible.
- stratify=y helps preserve the target class proportions in both sets.

K. Feature Scaling
- StandardScaler transforms features to have approximately zero mean and unit variance.
- fit_transform() learns scaling values from the training data and transforms it.
- transform() applies those same training scaling values to the test data.
- This avoids learning preprocessing information from the test set.

