## 8. VIVA QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS

Q1. What is data cleaning?
Ans. Data cleaning is the process of identifying and correcting missing, duplicate, inaccurate, or inconsistent data.

Q2. What is customer churn?
Ans. Customer churn occurs when a customer stops using a company's product or service.

Q3. What is the use of head()?
Ans. head() displays the first five rows of a DataFrame by default.

Q4. How are missing values identified?
Ans. isnull().sum() identifies and counts missing values in each column.

Q5. What is fillna()?
Ans. fillna() replaces missing values with a specified value or statistic.

Q6. Why are duplicate records removed?
Ans. Duplicates can cause repeated information and may affect analysis and model results.

Q7. What is IQR?
Ans. IQR stands for Interquartile Range. It is calculated as Q3 minus Q1.

Q8. What is an outlier?
Ans. An outlier is a value that is unusually far from most other observations.

Q9. What is the IQR rule for detecting outliers?
Ans. Values below Q1 - 1.5 × IQR or above Q3 + 1.5 × IQR are commonly treated as potential outliers.

Q10. What is feature engineering?
Ans. Feature engineering is the process of creating or modifying variables to make data more useful for analysis or machine learning.

Q11. What is the target variable in this program?
Ans. Churn is the target variable.

Q12. What is get_dummies()?
Ans. It converts categorical values into numerical indicator columns using one-hot encoding.

Q13. What is train_test_split()?
Ans. It divides a dataset into training and testing subsets.

Q14. Why is the dataset split into training and testing sets?
Ans. Training data is used to train a model, while testing data is used to evaluate its performance on unseen data.

Q15. What does test_size=0.2 mean?
Ans. It means 20% of the data is reserved for testing and 80% for training.

Q16. What is StandardScaler?
Ans. StandardScaler standardizes features by removing the mean and scaling to unit variance.

Q17. Why is stratify=y used?
Ans. It helps maintain the same approximate target-class proportions in the training and testing sets.

Q18. Why do we use fit_transform() on training data and transform() on test data?
Ans. The scaler learns parameters from training data only. The same parameters are then applied to test data to avoid data leakage.

